  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEA Boost project C6ote d&apos;Ivoire</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRCI staff and volunteers</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire, CRCI HQ and branches</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Community Engagement and Accountability (CEA) of the Croix-rouge C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There will be a strengthening of the existing community feedback system with the identification and popularization of collection mechanisms within communities. CEA focal points in local branches will be identified in order to bring back in a very short time, community feedback through digital tablets for some. Sessions to update the registration matrix will provide a credible database that corresponds to the concerns and needs of the communities. The coordination team will have this database to refine their operational strategies but share it with the communication team of the Ministry of Health after treatment.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project consists of two parts: 1) a series of training and awareness-raising activities for staff and volunteers on the integration of the Community, Engagement and Accountability in the implementation of their activities; and 2) insisting on the establishment of a community feedback system corresponding to the communities.</narrative>
  </description>
